  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs the lots LOT-096 (#188), LOT-151 (#241), we need a real, anonymized capture of this page state, so that the code is written against evidence, never a guess (LESSONS 35-36).\n\n### What to capture\n\nPost with a BMP emoji (e.g. U+2764) and with a variation selector (U+FE0F): kept, replaced or truncated?\n\nNote: write to a test topic or own MP: operator confirmation first\n\n### Read-only or write\n\n**Write capture**: it posts, deletes or sends something. Operator approval required before capturing (AGENTS.md §0).\n\n### Wanted by\n\n- LOT-096 (#188)\n- LOT-151 (#241)\n\n### Done when\n\n- [ ] Raw capture taken with the LOT-001 kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), anonymized, checked independently, committed under the fixtures tree with its MANIFEST entry.\n- [ ] The fact it settles is recorded in docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md (or the third-party notes of the LOT-071 spec for a non-HFR host), and each lot above is told on its issue.\n- [ ] A legacy oracle is added when a parser consumes the page (LOT-002..005 tooling).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/FIXTURES.md, tooling/fixtures/README.md, docs/lots/LOT-001-*.md (fixture kit and capture checklist), and docs/agents/LESSONS.md rows 33, 34, 36 and 39 (independent anonymization check, quote-aware patterns, skipped rows go back to the capture session, redaction by position). Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before capturing; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`. Captures are anonymized before commit and checked by an independent reviewer before any push; no cookie, `hash_check`, real pseudo or API key in any file. A write capture (anything that posts, deletes or sends) needs the operator's explicit approval first (AGENTS.md §0); use a throwaway account or own MP/test topic.",
